<div class="row" style="max-height: 65%; min-height: 65%;">
  <div class="col px-5">

    <div class="row" style="max-height: 20%; min-height: 20%;">
      <div class="col d-flex justify-content-start align-items-center">
        <h2 class="text-light-emphasis">
          Manual 
        </h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row" style="max-height: 65%; min-height: 65%;">
      <div class"col" style="min-width: 25%; max-width: 25%;">
        <nav id="navbar-example3" class="h-100 flex-column align-items-stretch pe-4 border-end">
          <nav class="nav nav-pills flex-column">
            <a class="nav-link text-warning" href="#help-customer-buttons">Customer tools</a>
            <nav class="nav nav-pills flex-column">
              <a class="nav-link ms-3 my-1 text-warning" href="#help-new-customer">Query tool</a>
            <a class="nav-link text-warning" href="#help-customer-tools">Customer tools</a>
            <nav class="nav nav-pills flex-column">
              <a class="nav-link ms-3 my-1 text-warning" href="#help-query">Query tool</a>
              <a class="nav-link ms-3 my-1 text-warning" href="#help-id">ID tool</a>
              <a class="nav-link ms-3 my-1 text-warning" href="#help-choose-file">Choose file tool</a>
              <a class="nav-link ms-3 my-1 text-warning" href="#help-api">Choose file tool</a>
            </nav>
          </nav>
        </nav>
      </div>

      <div class="col" style="min-width: 75%; max-width: 75%;">
        <div style="max-height: 45vh; min-height: 45vh; overflow-y: scroll;">
          <div id="help-customer-buttons">
            <h4 class="text-warning">Customer Buttons</h4>
          </div>
          <br>
          <div id="help-new-customer">
            <h5 class="text-warning">New Customer</h5>
            <p>
              By clicking on the new customer button the app will
              give you a form to fill out. After you submit the
              form, the customer will be created.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div id="help-customer-tools">
            <h4 class="text-warning">Customer tools</h4>
          </div>
          <br>
          <div id="help-query" class="w-75">
            <h5 class="text-warning">Query Tool:</h5>
            <p>
              This tool is used to make queries to the customers
              database.
            <p>
              By putting a valid column name in the first field
              and valid a column value on the second field the
              database will fetch and render the customers that
              correspond with these values.
            </p>
            <p>
              In case you put an invalid column name the app will
              give you an error. In case you put an invalid column
              value the database will fetch and render no entries.
              Here are the valid column names:
            </p>
            <table class="table table-hover">
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <th class="text-warning">first_name</th>
                  <td>string</td>
                  <th class="text-warning">last_name</th>
                  <td>string</td>
                  <th class="text-warning">email</th>
                  <td>string</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th class="text-warning">contact</th>
                  <td>string</td>
                  <th class="text-warning">date_of_birth</th>
                  <td>date</td>
                  <th class="text-warning">job</th>
                  <td>string</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th class="text-warning">marital</th>
                  <td>string</td>
                  <th class="text-warning">education</th>
                  <td>string</td>
                  <th class="text-warning">default</th>
                  <td>string</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th class="text-warning">loan</th>
                  <td>string</td>
                  <th class="text-warning">housing</th>
                  <td>string</td>
                  <th class="text-warning">balance</th>
                  <td>number</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th class="text-warning">calls</th>
                  <td>number</td>
                  <th class="text-warning">last_call</th>
                  <td>date</td>
                  <th class="text-warning">previous_calls</th>
                  <td>number</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th class="text-warning">previous_outcome</th>
                  <td>string</td>
                  <th class="text-warning">prediction</th>
                  <td>string</td>
                  <th class="text-warning">outcome</th>
                  <td>string</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <br>
          <div id="help-id">
            <h5 class="text-warning">ID Tool:</h5>
            <p>
              This tool is used to search for specific customers based on their id.
              After you provide the id of a customer, the app will render the customer's
              page.
            </p>
            <p>
              If you provide an id of a customer that does not exist, the app will give
              you an error.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div id="help-choose-file">
            <h5 class="text-warning">Choose File Tool:</h5>
            <p>
              This tool is used to import customer entries via a CSV file. By clicking the choose 
              file field the app will open your file explorer. When a file is choosen the field
              will display the file name. By clicking the import CSV button the app will import the
              customer entries from the CSV file and display them on the content view.
            </p>
            <p>
              In case your file is invalid the app will give you an error.
            </p>
            <h7 class="text-warning">Note:</h7>
            <p>
            If your CSV file contains rows with invalid values, the app will not import those
            rows.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div id="help-api">
            <h5 class="text-warning">API Tool</h5>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div> 
  </div>
</div>

